    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "DC-9\nSafety Instructions\nInstructions de Sécurité\nInstrucciones de Seguridad\nSicherheitsanleitungen\nUSAir",
      "FVACUATON PROCEDUKES\nPROCEDIMIENTOS DE EVACUACION\nEVAKUIERUNGSVERFAHREN\nPROCEDURES D'EVACUATION\nAHA\nAHA\nB\n6\nD\n0000\nExit Row Seating\n•\nSi usted está sentado en una fila de salida, y no\npuede leer, hablar o entender inglés, sirvase\ncontactar a un representante de UsAIro USAIr\nExpress para que se le cambie de astento.\n• Falls sich Ihr Sitz in einer Reihe an einem\nder Notausgänge befindet und wenn Sie weder\nEnglisch lesen, spreenen oder verstenen konnen,\nwenden Sie sich bitte an einen Vertreter von\nanderen Sitzplatz zuweisen wird.\nSi vous êtes assis près d'une issue de secours, et\nvous n'êtes pas en mesure de lire l'anglais, ni de le\nparler ou de le comprendre, veuillez contacter un\nreprésentant de la compagnie USAir ou USAir\nExpress pour obtenir un autre siege\nIf you are seated in an exit row, please review the\nfollowing. Federal Aviation Regulations require that\npassengers seated in this row meet the selection\ncriteria and are willing and able to operate the exit\nand assist others in the event of an emergency in\nwhich a crewmember is not available to do so.\nPlease identify the exit nearest to you and review the\ncorresponding functions found on this \"Safety\nInstructions\" card.\nPlease contact your Flight Attendant for reseating if\nyou have a condition, which is not apparent, that\nwould prevent you from performing the functions\nshown on this \"Safety Instructions\" card; would be\nharmed from doing so; do not wish to do so; or if\nany of the following apply:\n•\nMobility, strength or dexterity in both arms and\nhands. and both leas is not sumicientto derrorn\nthe functions and assist others, including:\n-Reaching the exit quickly\n-Reaching in every direction for mechanisms used\n-Securing the exit open\n-Removing obstructions (maintaining balance\nwhile doing so)\n-Quickly passing through the exit\n• You are less than 15 years old, require assistance\nfrom someone else to perform one or more of the\nfunctions, or would be prevented from doing so\nbecause of a condition or responsibility, such as\ncaring for a small child.\n• You cannot sufficiently impart information orally\nto others or understand oral crew commands.\n• You cannot read or understand the written and\norannie incrucions novice orrecute asssance\n(other than a hearing aid to hear or understand\ninstructions shouted by a crewmember.\n•You do not have the visual capacity to assess\nconditions outside of the exit or perform any other\nfunction described without the assistance of visual\naids other than contactlenses or evea asses\nIn the event of an emergency, follow the directions\nand hand signals of your crew. If a crewmember is\nnot available to assist you, follow the instructions on\nthe \"Safety Instructions\" card and posted signs. Wait\nuntil the airplane has stopped before opening the exit\nand look through the window, assessing conditions\n(looking for smoke, fire or obstructions) to\ndetermine whether it is safe to proceed. If it is safe to\ndo so, operate the exit and assist others according to\nthe instructions. Assess, select and follow a safe path\naway rom me aim ane.\nYour Flight Attendants will be glad to answer any\nquestions you may have.",
      "BRACE POSITIONS\nPOSICIONES PARA PROTECCION\nNOTLANDUNGEN\nPOSITIONS DE PROTECTION\nRESTRICTIONS\nRESTRICCIONES\nBESCHRÄNKUNGEN\nINTERDICTIONS\nWATER EVACUATION\nEVACUACION EN EL MAR\nEVAKUIERUNG ZU WASSER\nEVACUATION SUR L'EAU\nCopyright 01989 USAir\nDC9-3-ECPS\nC/C 190-0353\nRev. 8/93\n2002.127.650"
    ],
